# Drafted by Gemini (R15 lagoon), edited.

~ view
set lagoon_seen
if flag.crossroads_passage
cutscene dc_lagoon
Narrator: Out in the black mangrove lake sits a grand riverboat glowing with neon light, its tall iron funnels coughing plumes of magenta smoke into the night.
cutscene dc_lagoon_3
Narrator: A narrow coffin boat glides through the cypress roots toward the bank, poled by a silent chauffeur with green copper coins pressed over his eyes.
else
cutscene dc_lagoon_2
Narrator: Out in the mangrove lake, a rotted riverboat lies split in two upon the mud, a row of faded letters peeling from its waterlogged hull.
endif
cutscene end
-> END

~ wreck
Narrator: The broken stern settles deeper into the black silt with every ripple, smelling of wet char, swamp rot, and riverweed.
* [Investigation DC 12] Read the faded letters -> wreck_read | wreck_miss
* Leave it -> END

~ wreck_read
Narrator: Through the blistered paint and moss, you make out part of an old name: Dead M... H.... Without a token of passage, the grand boat is only a wreck.
-> END

~ wreck_miss
Narrator: The gilt lettering has peeled away in the damp, leaving only pale scars on the sodden timber that could spell almost anything.
-> END

~ wreck_ferryman
Narrator: The chauffeur stands motionless beside the landing with his pole planted in the mud, facing the dark water; whatever passenger he waits for, it is not you.
-> END

~ dock
Narrator: The chauffeur poles his long coffin boat quietly against the pilings and holds out one grey hand, copper coins dull upon his eyes and brow.
* Board the coffin boat -> board
* [if flag.ferryman_paid] Remind him you paid -> board
* Not yet -> END

~ board
Narrator: The narrow hull barely dips beneath your weight as the pole takes hold, pushing you out across the glassy black water toward the brass music and magenta glow.
set dc_boarded
quest withered_arm aboard
move dc_boat_promenade:from_gangplank

~ bellhops
if flag.crossroads_refused
bellhop_zombie [neutral]: Good evening, friends, and pardon the intrusion. My colleague and I have keen noses for the uninvited, and we can always smell a traveler without a token.
else
-> bh_ok
endif
* [Deception DC 16] We are expected -> bh_ok | bh_miss
* [if flag.ferryman_paid] The Ferryman vouched for us -> bh_ok
* [if gold >= 25] Tip them twenty-five gold -> bh_tip
* Fight the bellhops -> bh_fight

~ bh_ok
set dc_bellhops_ok
bellhop_zombie [smile]: Welcome aboard the Dead Man's Hand, honoured guests. Mind your step on the brass, and please enjoy one hundred gold of complimentary play at our tables tonight.
-> END

~ bh_miss
bellhop_zombie [smile]: That is a remarkably bold story, friend, and told with admirable posture, though I am afraid the guest list remains quite unconvinced.
-> bellhops

~ bh_tip
gold -25
set dc_bellhops_ok
Narrator: The heavy coins vanish into a velvet bellhop's bag no bigger than a teacup, and two vast dead men bow until their tiny hats nearly touch.
-> END

~ bh_fight
combat dc_bellhops
